        "original_id": "46209ea2-c8c2-5bc9-b0c8-528d997566f0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Warroad, Minnesota; Northwest Angle; Angle Township; Lake of the Woods County; Angle Inlet; Penasse; Magnusens Island\n- Radio Stations: KKWQ-FM; KRWB (AM)\n- Companies: Border Broadcasting\n- Historic Sites: Fort Saint Charles\n\nFacts:\n- KKWQ-FM 92.5 is a small local radio station broadcasting from the border town of Warroad, Minnesota.\n- The Northwest Angle, known locally as the Angle, is coextensive with Angle Township and is part of northern Lake of the Woods County, Minnesota.\n- KRWB (AM) is owned and operated by Border Broadcasting, and KKWQ-FM is its sister station.\n- Fort Saint Charles was located on Magnusens Island on the Northwest Angle of Minnesota, 3.5 miles east of Angle Inlet, Minnesota, and one mile southwest of Penasse, Minnesota, the state's most northerly point.",
